        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            <strong class="text-white">Fitness trackers usually count treadmill steps, because they
            count arm swing, not ground covered.</strong> Hold the rails or keep your hands still and
            the count collapses; a phone in your pocket copes better, and a phone on the console
            counts nothing.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Use an indoor workout mode, expect tracker and console distance to differ by a few percent,
            and calibrate the tracker to a belt you have checked. Trust the tracker for steps and the
            console for distance. For connecting a watch and syncing to Strava, see our guide to
            <a href="/how-to-connect-apple-watch-to-treadmill/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">connecting an Apple Watch to a treadmill</a>.
